      "**Great Mosque of Xi'an**\n\nOne of the oldest mosques in China (Tang dynasty origins, rebuilt Ming/Qing), it looks like a traditional Chinese temple from the outside—timber halls, glazed tiles, courtyards—while the qibla wall and mihrab orient worship toward Mecca. It demonstrates how Islamic space was integrated into Chinese urban and architectural norms.",
      "**Id Kah Mosque, Kashgar**\n\nThe Id Kah Mosque (15th century, with later expansions) is the largest in China and a symbol of Uyghur Islamic culture. Its yellow-tiled gate, domes, and minarets blend Central Asian and Chinese elements. Explore Id Kah and other Chinese-Islamic mosques on MosqueList.",
